-- title:
--   Consistency implies near-projectivity, strictly, at any positive bound δ on the inconsistency
-- statement:
--   A statement of the module `MIPRE.Background.QLD.Consistency` of the MIP\* = RE formalization (commit `70cbf1c` of vidick/MIPRE-formalization). From bipartite consistency to near-projectivity. The second half of blueprint `cor:ortho-from-consistency`. `Ortho.lean` turns *near-projectivity* of a POVM on Alice's factor into a projective measurement close to it; what the appendix has is *consistency* of Alice's POVM with one of Bob's. The bridge is a Cauchy--Schwarz step: writing `γ = ∑_{a ≠ b} ⟨ψ| Q_a ⊗ R_b |ψ⟩`, so that `∑_a ⟨ψ| Q_a ⊗ R_a |ψ⟩ = 1 - γ`, `1 - γ = ∑_a ⟨(Q_a ⊗ Id)ψ, (Id ⊗ R_a)ψ⟩ ≤ (∑_a ‖(Q_a ⊗ Id)ψ‖²)^{1/2} (∑_a ‖(Id ⊗ R_a)ψ‖²)^{1/2}` and the second factor is at most one because `∑_a R_a² ≤ ∑_a R_a = Id`.
--
--   **Consistency implies near-projectivity**, strictly, at any positive bound `δ` on the
--   inconsistency. This is the step the blueprint's proof calls a Cauchy--Schwarz step; the strictness
--   is the `γ²` slack in `(1 - γ)² = 1 - 2γ + γ²`, and it is what removes the compactness argument.
--
--   **Formal statement.** In Lean, with the scope shown:
--
--   ```lean
--   open MIPRE
--   open MIPRE.QLD
--   open Finset Matrix Kronecker MIPRE
--   open scoped ComplexOrder MatrixOrder
--   variable {A : Type*} [Fintype A] [DecidableEq A]
--   variable {dA dB : Type*} [Fintype dA] [DecidableEq dA] [Fintype dB] [DecidableEq dB]
--
--   theorem MIPRE.QLD.one_sub_two_mul_lt_sum_stateSqNorm {ψ : dA × dB → ℂ} (hψ : star ψ ⬝ᵥ ψ = 1)
--       (Q : POVM A dA) (R : POVM A dB) (δ : ℝ) (hδ : 0 < δ)
--       (hcons : pairInconsistency ψ Q R ≤ δ) :
--       1 - 2 * δ < ∑ a, stateSqNorm ψ (((Q.mats a).val))
--   ```
--
--   **Formalization Note** `MIPRE.QLD.one_sub_two_mul_lt_sum_stateSqNorm` is declared in `MIPRE/Background/QLD/Consistency.lean`, lines 149–189. The binders, hypotheses and conclusion are exactly those of the Lean statement above; the uploaded statement elaborates to the same type as the declaration in the repository. The definitions it mentions are those of the published definition bundles of the module's import closure.
